1
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,900
Thursday, the twelfth of June,

2
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:10,910
2025. Ahmedabad, Gujarat.

3
00:00:11,813 --> 00:00:13,783
The afternoon was hot and clear.

4
00:00:14,193 --> 00:00:16,803
Light winds. Six kilometres of visibility.

5
00:00:17,918 --> 00:00:20,658
At Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel International

6
00:00:20,658 --> 00:00:24,698
Airport, a Boeing 787 Dreamliner was being

7
00:00:24,698 --> 00:00:26,518
prepared for a long flight west,

8
00:00:26,518 --> 00:00:28,188
to London Gatwick.

9
00:00:28,939 --> 00:00:32,259
This is the story of Air India Flight 171,

10
00:00:32,259 --> 00:00:35,119
and of thirty-two seconds that are still

11
00:00:35,119 --> 00:00:36,349
not fully explained.

12
00:00:41,517 --> 00:00:43,337
Air India Flight 171.

13
00:00:43,337 --> 00:00:45,557
Two hundred and thirty passengers.

14
00:00:45,557 --> 00:00:46,747
Twelve crew.

15
00:00:47,338 --> 00:00:50,418
The aircraft, registered VT-ANB,

16
00:00:50,418 --> 00:00:52,988
had flown with Air India since 2014.

17
00:00:53,768 --> 00:00:56,338
In the cockpit sat an experienced crew.

18
00:00:56,848 --> 00:01:00,338
The captain had logged around 15,600 hours.

19
00:01:00,788 --> 00:01:04,090
The first officer, around 3,400.

20
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:07,280
The jet was cleared for a full-length takeoff

21
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:08,750
from runway 23.

22
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:12,296
After a 62-second takeoff roll,

23
00:01:12,296 --> 00:01:15,606
at 1:38 and 39 seconds in the afternoon,

24
00:01:16,096 --> 00:01:18,366
Flight 171 left the ground.

25
00:01:19,589 --> 00:01:22,619
Three seconds later, at 180 knots,

26
00:01:22,989 --> 00:01:25,799
the flight recorder logged something extraordinary.

27
00:01:26,621 --> 00:01:28,981
Both engine fuel control switches moved

28
00:01:28,981 --> 00:01:31,461
from RUN to CUTOFF.

29
00:01:31,461 --> 00:01:32,611
One after the other.

30
00:01:32,961 --> 00:01:33,951
One second apart.

31
00:01:35,039 --> 00:01:36,689
Fuel to both engines stopped.

32
00:01:37,059 --> 00:01:38,629
Thrust began to fall away.

33
00:01:39,179 --> 00:01:40,289
The ram air turbine,

34
00:01:40,679 --> 00:01:42,869
the aircraft's emergency power source,

35
00:01:43,219 --> 00:01:44,632
dropped into the airstream.

36
00:01:45,182 --> 00:01:46,832
On the cockpit voice recording,

37
00:01:47,322 --> 00:01:49,902
one pilot asks the other why he cut off

38
00:01:49,902 --> 00:01:52,262
the fuel. The other replies that he did

39
00:01:52,262 --> 00:01:52,712
not.

40
00:01:53,543 --> 00:01:55,503
Ten seconds after the cutoff,

41
00:01:55,503 --> 00:01:57,973
the first switch was moved back to RUN.

42
00:01:58,483 --> 00:02:00,233
Four seconds later, the second.

43
00:02:00,563 --> 00:02:02,953
The engines began trying to relight.

44
00:02:03,503 --> 00:02:04,933
Then, a mayday call.

45
00:02:05,283 --> 00:02:06,233
A loss of thrust.

46
00:02:06,743 --> 00:02:08,523
The controller asked for the flight's call

47
00:02:08,523 --> 00:02:10,273
sign. There was no reply.

48
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,310
Thirty-two seconds after takeoff,

49
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,230
at 13:39 and 11 seconds,

50
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,690
the recordings stopped.

51
00:02:19,888 --> 00:02:24,128
Flight 171 came down 1.7 kilometres from

52
00:02:24,128 --> 00:02:26,528
the runway, onto the hostel buildings of

53
00:02:26,528 --> 00:02:30,258
B.J. Medical College, in Meghani Nagar.

54
00:02:30,898 --> 00:02:34,848
It was lunchtime. Of the 242 people on board,

55
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:38,158
241 were killed. On the ground,

56
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:40,298
nineteen more lost their lives,

57
00:02:40,298 --> 00:02:42,988
and 67 were seriously injured.

58
00:02:44,016 --> 00:02:46,716
One passenger survived. He had been sitting

59
00:02:46,716 --> 00:02:50,386
in seat 11A, beside an emergency exit.

60
00:02:51,042 --> 00:02:54,242
Hundreds of firefighters, soldiers and disaster

61
00:02:54,242 --> 00:02:56,732
response teams were sent to the site.

62
00:02:58,035 --> 00:03:00,475
India's Aircraft Accident Investigation

63
00:03:00,475 --> 00:03:02,805
Bureau led the inquiry,

64
00:03:03,275 --> 00:03:05,905
assisted by British and American investigators.

65
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:08,779
Both flight recorders were recovered.

66
00:03:09,329 --> 00:03:11,789
A month later, the preliminary report set

67
00:03:11,789 --> 00:03:13,299
out what the switches did,

68
00:03:13,629 --> 00:03:14,339
but not why.

69
00:03:15,164 --> 00:03:17,054
It found no mechanical fault.

70
00:03:17,544 --> 00:03:19,924
It made no safety recommendations for Boeing,

71
00:03:19,924 --> 00:03:21,524
or for the engine maker,

72
00:03:21,524 --> 00:03:22,621
GE.

73
00:03:23,071 --> 00:03:27,051
In 2018, the US regulator had advised operators

74
00:03:27,051 --> 00:03:29,701
to inspect the switches' locking feature.

75
00:03:30,271 --> 00:03:31,711
Air India had not done so,

76
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:34,081
because the advice was not mandatory.

77
00:03:34,871 --> 00:03:36,891
Later inspections of its fleet found no

78
00:03:36,891 --> 00:03:37,381
problems.

79
00:03:38,317 --> 00:03:39,847
At the time of this film,

80
00:03:40,117 --> 00:03:42,427
the final report had not been made public.

81
00:03:44,261 --> 00:03:45,721
Two hundred and sixty lives.

82
00:03:45,721 --> 00:03:47,271
Thirty-two seconds.

83
00:03:48,218 --> 00:03:50,658
And a question that their families are still

84
00:03:50,658 --> 00:03:52,068
waiting to have answered.

